],"pub":["Nacon"],"released":"Oct 7, 2016","meta":68,"langs":["English","French","Italian","German","Spanish - Spain","Polish","Korean","Simplified Chinese"],"min":[["OS","Windows\u00ae 7 64bits"],["Processor","Intel\u00ae Core i3 / AMD Phenom\u2122 II X2"],["Memory","4 GB RAM"],["Graphics","NVIDIA\u00ae GeForce\u00ae GTX 650 / AMD Radeon\u2122 HD 7750"],["DirectX","Version 11"],["Storage","20 GB available space"],["Sound Card","DirectX Compatible Soundcard"]],"rec":[["OS","Windows\u00ae 10 64bits"],["Processor","Intel\u00ae Core i5 / AMD FX 8150"],["Memory","8 GB RAM"],["Graphics","NVIDIA\u00ae GeForce\u00ae GTX 780 / AMD Radeon\u2122 R9 290 2 GB"],["DirectX","Version 11"],["Network","Broadband Internet connection"],["Storage","20 GB available space"]],"deck":1,"blurb":"Rally racing here means running timed stages one car at a time against the clock on gravel, tarmac and snow, with a co-driver reading pace notes while weather, night sections and mechanical failures keep changing the job. It covers the official 2016 season, including Rally China and the Super Special Stages, with the licensed cars and drivers.\n\nBeyond the career, you can take on weekly online challenges and global leaderboards, or share a screen for local split-screen races. Full controller support makes it comfortable on a gamepad. It fits players who enjoy simulation-leaning driving, learning tracks and trimming seconds, and it is about precision and survival more than wheel-to-wheel racing."}}